<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>About Us | Legal Rights Explained</title>
    <style>
      * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
      body { font-family: Georgia, serif; background: #f0f4f8; }
      header { background: #1a3a5c; padding: 28px 20px; text-align: center; border-bottom: 3px solid #c9a84c; }
      .header-tag { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 3px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #c9a84c; margin-bottom: 6px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; }
      header h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; color: white; font-weight: normal; }
      nav { background: #152d47; display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 28px; padding: 10px; }
      nav a { color: #a8c4e0; font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 1px; text-transform: uppercase; text-decoration: none; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; }
      nav a:hover { color: #c9a84c; }
      main { max-width: 760px; margin: 36px auto; padding: 0 16px; }
      .card { background: white; border-radius: 12px; padding: 36px; box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.07); border: 0.5px solid #dde3ea; margin-bottom: 16px; }
      .page-title { font-size: 1.4rem; color: #1a3a5c; margin-bottom: 6px; }
      .subtitle { font-size: 14px; color: #aaa; margin-bottom: 28px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; border-bottom: 0.5px solid #eee; padding-bottom: 16px; }
      h2 { color: #1a3a5c; margin: 24px 0 8px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.5px; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 12px; }
      p { color: #555; line-height: 1.9; font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
      .values { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 14px; margin-top: 16px; }
      .value-item { background: #f8fafc; border: 0.5px solid #dde3ea; border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px; text-align: center; }
      .value-icon { font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 8px; }
      .value-title { font-size: 13px; font-weight: bold; color: #1a3a5c; margin-bottom: 4px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; }
      .value-text { font-size: 12px; color: #888; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; }
      .mission { background: #1a3a5c; border-radius: 12px; padding: 28px; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 16px; }
      .mission h2 { color: #c9a84c; margin-bottom: 12px; }
      .mission p { color: #a8c4e0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.9; }
      footer { text-align: center; color: #aaa; font-size: 12px; padding: 28px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; }
      footer a { color: #aaa; margin: 0 8px; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header>
      <div class="header-tag">⚖ US Legal Information</div>
      <h1>Legal Rights Explained</h1>
    </header>
    <nav>
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <a href="/about">About</a>
      <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>
      <a href="/terms">Terms</a>
      <a href="/contact">Contact</a>
    </nav>
    <main>

      <div class="mission">
        <h2>OUR MISSION</h2>
        <p>"To make legal information accessible to every American, regardless of their background or income — in plain, simple English."</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h1 class="page-title">About Us</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">Making legal information accessible to everyone</p>

        <h2>Who We Are</h2>
        <p>Legal Rights Explained is a free online resource dedicated to helping everyday Americans understand their legal rights. We believe that everyone deserves access to clear, simple legal information — not just those who can afford expensive lawyers.</p>

        <h2>What We Do</h2>
        <p>We use artificial intelligence to take complex legal questions and translate them into plain, simple English. Our tool covers all 50 US states and provides answers tailored to your specific location, so you always get relevant information.</p>

        <h2>Why We Built This</h2>
        <p>Most people who search for legal information online end up more confused than when they started. Legal websites are full of jargon, outdated information, and generic answers that don't apply to their state. We built Legal Rights Explained to solve exactly that problem.</p>

        <h2>Our Values</h2>
        <div class="values">
          <div class="value-item">
            <div class="value-icon">⚖️</div>
            <div class="value-title">Clarity</div>
            <div class="value-text">We explain legal concepts in plain English anyone can understand</div>
          </div>
          <div class="value-item">
            <div class="value-icon">🔒</div>
            <div class="value-title">Privacy</div>
            <div class="value-text">We don't store your questions or sell your data to anyone</div>
          </div>
          <div class="value-item">
            <div class="value-icon">🌎</div>
            <div class="value-title">Access</div>
            <div class="value-text">Free legal information for every American in every state</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 style="margin-top:24px;">Important Disclaimer</h2>
        <p>Legal Rights Explained provides general legal information only. Nothing on this website constitutes legal advice or creates an attorney-client relationship. For advice specific to your situation, always consult a licensed attorney in your state.</p>
      </div>

    </main>
    <footer>
      <p>© 2026 LegalRightsExplained.com — Not a substitute for professional legal advice</p>
      <p style="margin-top:8px;">
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
        <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>
        <a href="/contact">Contact</a>
      </p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>